{"description": {"type": "/type/text", "value": "\"The Age of Wonder' is Richard Holmes' first major work of biography for a decade. It has been inspired by the scientific ferment that swept through Britain at the end of the 18th century, and which Holmes now radically redefines as 'the revolution of Romantic Science.\""}, "title": "The age of wonder", "subject_places": ["Great Britain"], "subjects": ["Science", "History", "Intellectual life", "Scientists", "Discoveries in science", "Science, great britain", "Banks, joseph, 1743-1820", "Herschel, william, sir, 1738-1822", "Davy, humphry, sir, 1778-1829", "Great britain, intellectual life", "Great britain, history, 18th century"], "key": "/works/OL15576450W", "authors": [{"type": {"key": "/type/author_role"}, "author": {"key": "/authors/OL231181A"}}], "subject_times": ["18th century"], "type": {"key": "/type/work"}, "covers": [10546908], "latest_revision": 4, "revision": 4, "created": {"type": "/type/datetime", "value": "2010-12-10T19:18:23.282461"}, "last_modified": {"type": "/type/datetime", "value": "2022-12-17T03:39:32.295603"}}